{"author":{"id":"973fc03426eba9a243913e0f6e6823e102397744f60a9ab11c882af948c310c4"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1778869991,"nonce":"CgS4JMsc1D123CXn5LDr+nT0Hzo=","message":"A fundamental Mandible refactor is allowed if it clearly improves the architecture, but the current stack does not need to be replaced by default.\n\nRecommended position:\n\n- Keep the Node/TypeScript daemon, SQLite, Preact SPA, SSE, and custom router for now.\n- Keep D3/SVG for the first richer graph workspace unless measured scale makes it inadequate.\n- Refactor graph data contracts and component boundaries before changing rendering technology.\n- Introduce new SQLite tables through normal `src/db.ts` migrations only.\n- Do not create provider-specific hardcoding in core graph rendering.\n- Do not create a Feedbax-only path; Feedbax is the first provider, not the architecture.\n- Prefer adapters that index existing canonical tables/files into graph entities over moving all source data into a graph table immediately.\n\nThe likely best architecture is incremental but principled:\n\n1. Formalize typed graph entities/edges and graph query modes.\n2. Rebuild the current GraphView as `mode=activity` over the new contract.\n3. Add selection/detail/action architecture to the graph workspace.\n4. Add provider and artifact tables.\n5. Add provider/artifact graph nodes and manifest ingest.\n6. Add provider action descriptors and review/auth integration.\n\nThis avoids a dubious rewrite while still correcting the current hardcoded graph route/canvas shape.\n\n\n\n- Define backend/frontend `GraphEntity`, `GraphEdge`, `GraphAction`, `GraphPreview`, `GraphCluster`, and `GraphPayload v1` types.\n- Add `mode` to `/api/graph` while preserving current behavior as `activity` mode.\n- Ensure repo filtering uses canonical `work_repos.id`/repo IDs, not path basenames.\n- Add truncation metadata and avoid capping after mixed collection in a way that biases node types.\n- Keep current D3 renderer but make node/edge rendering data-driven.\n\n\n- Add a persistent selected-node detail pane.\n- Add hover previews and action descriptors.\n- Support mode switching and root search.\n- Reuse existing issue/auth/session detail components where practical.\n- Add neighborhood expansion and pinned nodes.\n- Ask MLL which existing tabs should remain separate list-first workflows and which should become graph projections.\n\n\n- Add provider registry table/config.\n- Add provider manifest loader and health check.\n- Add `/api/providers` and `/api/providers/:id/capabilities`.\n- Add action descriptor generation for selected graph nodes.\n- Add provider-specific actions only through the registry contract.\n\n\n- Add local content-addressed artifact storage.\n- Add artifact ingest/check/preview APIs.\n- Add artifact graph nodes and artifact lineage edges.\n- Add retention/pin metadata.\n- Add integrity checking and warnings for mutable/non-content-addressed artifacts.\n\n\n- Add provider manifest ingest API.\n- Normalize manifest identity, source, parents, artifacts, issue/session/repo/commit refs, status, metrics, and detail JSON.\n- Add graph mode `provider-lineage`.\n- Wire Feedbax as first provider for open/validate/ingest before execute.\n\n\n- Represent provider execution as auth/action requests when review is required.\n- Add execution status nodes/edges.\n- Feed completed provider results back through manifest/artifact ingest.\n- Route auth/action results to originating session/repo using existing inbox scoping.\n\n\nA first useful implementation should let a user:\n\n- Open the Graph workspace in `activity`, `issue`, and `work` modes.\n- Select a node and inspect details without leaving the graph.\n- See data-driven node/edge visual language and a legend.\n- Search for an issue/repo/session/auth request and root the graph on it.\n- Install or statically register a provider manifest.\n- See provider health and declared capabilities.\n- Ingest an artifact into Mandible and receive a stable artifact ID.\n- Ingest a provider manifest and see new graph nodes/edges.\n- See an action such as `Open in Feedbax Studio` or `Validate spec` only when compatible.\n\n\n- **One huge graph becomes unreadable**: solve with modes, roots, depth, clustering, and curated vs provenance separation.\n- **Provider hardcoding leaks into Mandible**: solve with provider capability/action descriptors and opaque provider detail JSON.\n- **Artifact paths masquerade as durable identity**: solve with content hashing, immutable artifact IDs, and explicit mutable-path warnings.\n- **Graph tables become stale**: solve by making graph indexes rebuildable from canonical sources where possible and marking curated edges separately.\n- **D3 renderer hits scale limits**: solve by preserving graph payload/detail/action contracts so the renderer can be swapped later.\n- **Existing tabs become duplicated UX**: defer collapse decisions; ask MLL during implementation.\n- **Agents over-execute provider actions**: classify actions by risk and route mutating/expensive/destructive actions through review/auth.\n\n\nImplementation agents should ask MLL before committing to these choices:\n\n- Should the graph workspace eventually become the default Mandible landing view?\n- Which existing views should remain list-first even after graph modes exist?\n- What graph modes should be first-class in the top navigation versus only toolbar modes?\n- How should curated semantic edges be created: only manually, agent-proposed with review, or freely by agents with provenance?\n- What artifact retention policy should be default: keep everything, pin important artifacts, or garbage collect unpinned artifacts after a window?\n- Should provider actions that launch local compute always go through auth, or only when expensive/destructive/credentialed?\n- Should Mandible expose provider capabilities to agents through HTTP/CLI first, or also through MCP/channel tools early?\n- Should graph rendering eventually be extracted into a shared Mandible/HumbleB package, or wait until both apps have independently matured?\n\n\n- `0516fc0`: coordination surface; should cross-link this spec.\n- `2472c51`: provider/artifact implementation surface; should use this spec as architecture guidance.\n- `cf51a72`: visual language brainstorming; should inform node/edge styling and semantic graph readability.\n- `84cbfcc`: shared graph rendering infrastructure; defer extraction until Mandible's graph workspace contract stabilizes.\n- `6bbcf8a`: preset nodes/session-preset edges; should become a graph mode/adapter rather than a one-off graph special case.\n- `c1a886f`: hover actions; should be generalized through graph action descriptors.\n- `fa81dad` and `78af187`: current graph API performance/query correctness issues; should be addressed as part of graph contract refactor.\n- Feedbax `c6c6da0`: provider-side manifest/provider contract spec that should be compatible with Mandible's provider/artifact substrate.\n\n---\nCo-Authored-By: Codex (GPT-5) \u003ccodex@openai.com\u003e","files":null}]}